{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:15804236 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:15804236 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"15804236","source":"MED","pmid":"15804236","pmcid":"PMC1180725","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC1180725"]},"doi":"10.1042/bj20050083","title":"Characterization of mouse amino acid transporter B0AT1 (slc6a19).","authorString":"Böhmer C, Bröer A, Munzinger M, Kowalczuk S, Rasko JE, Lang F, Bröer S.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Böhmer C","firstName":"Christoph","lastName":"Böhmer","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Physiologisches Institut, Universität Tübingen, 72076 Tübingen, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Bröer A","firstName":"Angelika","lastName":"Bröer","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Munzinger M","firstName":"Michael","lastName":"Munzinger","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Kowalczuk S","firstName":"Sonja","lastName":"Kowalczuk","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3787-3505"}},{"fullName":"Rasko JE","firstName":"John E J","lastName":"Rasko","initials":"JE","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2975-807X"}},{"fullName":"Lang F","firstName":"Florian","lastName":"Lang","initials":"F"},{"fullName":"Bröer S","firstName":"Stefan","lastName":"Bröer","initials":"S"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3787-3505"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8040-1634"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2975-807X"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"Pt 3","volume":"389","journalIssueId":1242900,"dateOfPublication":"2005 Aug","monthOfPublication":8,"yearOfPublication":2005,"printPublicationDate":"2005-08-01","journal":{"title":"The Biochemical journal","medlineAbbreviation":"Biochem J","issn":"0264-6021","nlmid":"2984726R","isoabbreviation":"Biochem J","essn":"1470-8728"}},"pubYear":"2005","pageInfo":"745-751","abstractText":"The mechanism of the mouse (m)B0AT1 (slc6a19) transporter was studied in detail using two electrode voltage-clamp techniques and tracer studies in the Xenopus oocyte expression system. All neutral amino acids induced inward currents at physiological potentials, but large neutral non-aromatic amino acids were the preferred substrates of mB0AT1. Substrates were transported with K0.5 values ranging from approx. 1 mM to approx. 10 mM. The transporter mediates Na+-amino acid co-transport with a stoichiometry of 1:1. No other ions were involved in the transport mechanism. An increase in the extracellular Na+ concentration reduced the K0.5 for leucine, and vice versa. Moreover, the K0.5 values and Vmax values of both substrates varied with the membrane potential. As a result, K0.5 and Vmax values are a complex function of the concentration of substrate and co-substrate and the membrane potential. A model is presented assuming random binding order and a positive charge associated with the ternary [Na+-substrate-transporter] complex, which is consistent with the experimental data.","affiliation":"Physiologisches Institut, Universität Tübingen, 72076 Tübingen, Germany.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Oocytes"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Xenopus"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Amino Acids","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Amino Acid Transport Systems","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","